---
title: Experience collection
layout: home
description: Things that happened — where, when, and what it was like. A photograph each, the number of the thing in its corner, and no attempt to make any of it sound like a CV.
eyebrow: Collections · Experience
source: src/components/life.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Experience · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap-wide" data-sidebar="on">
	<article class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 2rem">
		<header class="im-collhead im-collhead-patterned">
			<span class="im-collhead-art im-bg-rings" style="--im-art: #06b6d4" aria-hidden="true"></span>
			<p class="im-eyebrow">Experience</p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title">Things I have done</h1>
			<p class="im-collhead-text">Not work. The other kind — water, cold, distance, and a few hours of being usefully frightened. Everything here has a date because everything here happened.</p>
			<p class="im-collhead-meta"><span>{{demo.experience.length}} of them</span><span>{{demo.expgroups.length}} kinds</span><span>Since 2023</span><a href="/collections/wishlist/">The list they came from</a></p>
		</header>

		<div class="im-collbar">
			<div class="im-collbar-filters">
				<a class="im-tag" href="#exps" aria-current="page">Everything</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#exps">Water</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#exps">Cold</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#exps">Distance</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#exps">Height</a>
			</div>
			<div class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: .375rem">
				<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm" type="button">{{icon "list-filter"}}Most recent</button>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="im-stack" id="exps" style="--im-stack-gap: 2.25rem">
			{{#each demo.expgroups}}
			<section class="im-usegroup">
				<header class="im-usegroup-head">
					<h2 class="im-usegroup-title">{{icon mark}}{{name}}</h2>
					<p class="im-usegroup-text">{{text}}</p>
				</header>
				{{!-- A carousel, not a grid: a group has two or three things in
					  it and a grid of three leaves a hole where the fourth would
					  be. Sideways, they read as a set. --}}
				{{#> "components/carousel" label=name dots=true style="--im-slides: 1.15; --im-slides-sm: 1.8; --im-slides-md: 2.4"}}
					{{#each items}}
					<article class="im-exp">
						<span class="im-exp-media">
							<img src="{{lookup @root.demo.shots shot}}" alt="" loading="lazy">
							<span class="im-exp-figure">{{figure}}<small>{{unit}}</small></span>
							{{#if badge}}<span class="im-kind im-kind-over" data-kind="issue">{{icon "sparkles"}}{{badge}}</span>{{/if}}
						</span>
						<div class="im-exp-body">
							<p class="im-exp-where"><span>{{where}}</span><span>{{when}}</span></p>
							<h3 class="im-exp-title"><a href="/collections/experience/page/">{{title}}</a></h3>
							<p class="im-exp-text">{{text}}</p>
							<p><span class="im-kind" data-kind="tag">{{icon "compass"}}{{kind}}</span></p>
						</div>
					</article>
					{{/each}}
				{{/"components/carousel"}}
			</section>
			{{/each}}
		</div>
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail">
		<div class="im-widgets">
			<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="ew-sum">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="ew-sum">So far</h2>
				<div class="im-widget-stats">
					<div><strong>{{demo.experience.length}}</strong><span>Done</span></div>
					<div><strong>6</strong><span>Countries</span></div>
					<div><strong>2023</strong><span>Since</span></div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="ew-next">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="ew-next">Next on the list <a href="/collections/wishlist/">All</a></h2>
				<ul class="im-widget-list">
					{{#foreach demo.wishlist}}{{#match @number "<" 4}}<li><a href="/collections/wishlist/">{{title}}<small>{{#if where}}{{where}}{{else}}Someday{{/if}}</small></a></li>{{/match}}{{/foreach}}
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="ew-trips">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="ew-trips">The trips they came from <a href="/collections/travel/">Travel</a></h2>
				<ul class="im-widget-list">
					{{#foreach demo.trips}}{{#match @number "<" 3}}<li><a href="/collections/travel/trip/">{{title}}<small>{{country}} · {{when}}</small></a></li>{{/match}}{{/foreach}}
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="ew-gear">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="ew-gear">What it took <a href="/collections/uses/">Uses</a></h2>
				<div class="im-widget-products">
					{{#foreach demo.uses}}{{#match @number "<" 3}}<a class="im-widget-product" href="/collections/uses/page/"><span class="im-widget-product-mark">{{@number}}</span><span class="im-widget-product-name">{{title}}</span>{{icon "arrow-right"}}</a>{{/match}}{{/foreach}}
				</div>
			</section>
			<aside class="im-ad im-ad-rectangle" aria-label="Advertisement">
				<span class="im-ad-label">Sponsored</span>
				<span class="im-ad-slot"><img src="{{demo.shots.[5]}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
				<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-ad-remove" type="button" popovertarget="ad-gate">{{icon "circle-x"}}Remove ads</button>
			</aside>
		</div>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>The number goes on the picture</h2>
		<p>Thirty metres. Four thousand metres. Forty-two point two kilometres. Two degrees. Whatever the thing is <em>measured</em> in is the first question anybody asks about it, so it sits in the corner of the photograph in the mono face — <code>im-exp-figure</code> — where a video card would put its length.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>im-exp</code></td><td>The card. It fills on hover with a panel behind it, like every other card in the system.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-exp-figure</code></td><td>The measurement, bottom left of the picture. A number and a unit, nothing else.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-exp-where</code></td><td>Place, then date, with the drawn dot between them.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-exps</code></td><td>The grid, at <code>--im-exps-min</code> (18rem) with a taller row gap than column gap.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>

		<h2>It is the other half of the bucket list</h2>
		<p>An experience is a <a href="/collections/wishlist/">bucket-list</a> item that came true, so the two collections are deliberately one shape in two tenses. A done row in the list links here; this page links back to the list it came from. Neither of them is a blog post about how it felt — that is the <a href="/collections/post/">post collection</a>, and it should be linked to, not inlined.</p>

		<h2>Rules</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>One photograph, taken there.</strong> A stock image of scuba diving on a page about your dive is the fastest way to make the whole page look invented.</li>
			<li><strong>Numbers, not adjectives.</strong> "30m" says more than "deep", and it is checkable.</li>
			<li><strong>Do not rank them.</strong> A five-star rating on a life experience is a strange thing to publish and a stranger thing to read.</li>
			<li><strong>Keep the frightening ones.</strong> The two-degree swim is the reason anybody reads to the bottom.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>
